  "id": "auditory-training",
  "term": "auditory training",
  "definition": "Auditory training is practice designed to help people cope with a degraded or hard-to-hear sound signal. In the supplied source, it is described as improving listening-related functioning in adults with hearing loss, especially when auditory tasks also engage broader cognitive skills such as attention or working memory.",
