      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that the packet describes auditory training as improving listening-related functioning in adults with hearing loss—this is supported—but it also specifies that this is especially true “when auditory tasks also engage broader cognitive skills such as attention or working memory.” The packet explicitly discusses working memory training and relates outcomes to executive functions, but it does not clearly mention “attention” by name as a cognitive skill in the described training context.",
        "Because “attention” is an unsupported specific example in the definition relative to the packet text, the definition contains a substantive claim not defensibly supported by the provided source."
